            <ArticleTitle>Successful management of coronary artery perforation with helical platinum microcoil embolization.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>320-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of small coronary artery perforation during coronary intervention is presented. Continued leakage occurred despite prolonged intracoronary balloon inflation, in part probably related to the use of glycoprotein (GP) IIB/IIIA inhibitors. It was successfully managed by microcoil embolization without any sequel, helping avoid surgery in a high-risk patient. Cathet. Cardiovasc. Intervent. 51:320-322, 2000.</AbstractText>
